		<title type="html"><![CDATA[New DANCE code available 012109]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=12230#p12230"><![CDATA[
I have posted a new version of DANCE with updated code at:<br><br><a href="http://www.magix.ucla.edu/dance/#download" class="postlink">http://www.magix.ucla.edu/dance/#download</a><br><br>The new version is: dance_v4_012109.zip<br><br>DANCE is a software package for physics-based character animation. One of its goals is to provide researchers with a common platform where they can test their control methods and share their results. In addition, it provides the common, yet complex functionality that everyone needs in a physics-based animation system, allowing researchers to concentrate on their research work. DANCE has been used for a variety of physics-based applications that include biomechanics modelling and composeable controllers.<br><br>This version contains:<br><br>1) Builds on Window, Linux, OsX<br>2) Scriptable controllers (use Python to write controllers)<br>3) Non-linear editor for controllers<br>4) Attachments<br>5) Some bug fixes<br>6) Updated manual<br><br>I appreciate any feedback about making sure that the code<br>builds and runs properly.<br><br>Regards,<br><br>Ari Shapiro<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2150">ashapiro</a> — Thu Jan 22, 2009 8:01 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
